      "scoring": "Task-normalized average pass@1: the 3 attempts are averaged per task, then task scores are averaged so every task has equal weight. All component outcomes are binary. Index is a simple average of the 3 component scores.",
      "measures": [
        "index score",
        "cost per task (USD)",
        "token usage by input/cache/cache-write/reasoning/output",
        "wall-clock time per task"
      ],
      "cost_methodology": "Average pay-per-token API cost per task using provider token pricing, with cached input priced separately from uncached input and cache-write charges included where providers bill for them. Not consumer plan pricing.",
      "source_url": "https://artificialanalysis.ai/agents/coding-agents",
      "methodology_url": "https://artificialanalysis.ai/methodology/coding-agents-benchmarking",
      "terms_url": "https://artificialanalysiscdn.com/legal/ProDataPlatformTerms.pdf",
      "last_verified": "2026-08-21",
      "verified_via": "live page read in-browser; the leaderboard table is client-rendered and is not visible to plain HTTP fetch",
      "redistributable": false,
      "attribution": "Source: Artificial Analysis (artificialanalysis.ai)",
      "attribution_url": "https://artificialanalysis.ai/agents/coding-agents",
      "attribution_note": "Exact string and hyperlink required by the Data Platform Terms, section 5. Do not paraphrase.",
      "covers_current_models": true,
      "caveats": [
        "Rows are HARNESS + MODEL combinations, not bare models. Claude Code + Opus 5 is not the same measurement as Opus 5 in another harness; AA's own harness comparison shows the harness materially changes the score. Never present an AA figure as a property of the model alone.",
        "Index scores are read from the published chart as 0-100 composite values. Solvency derives pass_rate = index / 100 on the basis that the index is an average of task-normalized pass@1 rates. This derivation is an INTERPRETATION, flagged per row as pass_rate_derivation.",
        "Per-model token counts are published as charts only; numeric values were not captured, so Solvency cannot recompute AA's cost at current prices. AA's cost is carried as measured, at AA's pricing snapshot.",
        "AA notes prompt cache hit rates vary significantly by provider routing, which can materially change effective cost."
      ],
